---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import JsonLd from '@/components/JsonLd.astro';
import {
  getGameConfig,
  generateBreadcrumbSchema,
} from '@/lib/data';

const config = getGameConfig();

const breadcrumbSchema = generateBreadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Puzzle Guide', url: '/puzzle-guide/' },
]);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Dread Disc Puzzle Guide - Mechanics, Hints & Solutions"
  description="Dread Disc puzzle guide covering spot-the-difference mechanics, observation strategies, spoiler-free hints, and puzzle-solving tips for the demo."
>
  <JsonLd schema={breadcrumbSchema} />

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-red-400 transition-colors">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-2">›</span>
      <span class="text-gray-300">Puzzle Guide</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold mb-4 text-gray-100">
      Dread Disc Puzzle Guide
    </h1>

    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
      Understanding Dread Disc's puzzle mechanics is key to surviving. This guide explains the core systems
      and provides progressively revealing hints so you can solve puzzles without full spoilers.
    </p>

    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-8">
      <span class="text-xs bg-green-900/30 text-green-400 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-green-700/40">✓ Verified in demo</span>
      <span class="text-xs bg-gray-800 text-gray-400 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Demo Content</span>
    </div>

    <!-- Core Mechanics -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6 text-gray-200">Core Puzzle Mechanics</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="bg-gray-800/50 border border-gray-700/50 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-200 mb-2">🔍 Spot-the-Difference Loop</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
            The fundamental loop: enter the apartment, observe the current state, leave, re-enter, and identify what changed.
            Changes range from subtle (a shifted pillow) to dramatic (a new door appearing). The game tracks which differences you correctly identify.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-800/50 border border-gray-700/50 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-200 mb-2">🚪 Door & Window Security</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
            In parallel with spotting differences, you must secure every door and window. The puzzle interweaves observation with security —
            some differences involve door/window state changes, creating a dual challenge.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-800/50 border border-gray-700/50 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-200 mb-2">🎲 Randomized Elements</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
            Each playthrough randomizes which differences appear. You cannot memorize a fixed set of changes —
            you must develop genuine observation skills. Some differences are guaranteed, others vary.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-800/50 border border-gray-700/50 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-200 mb-2">📈 Escalation</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
            Each cycle introduces more differences and higher-stakes changes. Early cycles might have 1–3 subtle changes.
            Later cycles can feature 4–6+ changes including new objects, damaged items, and environmental shifts.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Progressive Hints -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6 text-gray-200">Hint Sections (No Spoilers)</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <details class="group border border-gray-700/50 rounded-lg bg-gray-800/30">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-4 cursor-pointer font-medium hover:bg-gray-800/50 transition-colors text-gray-200">
            <span>Hint: How many differences should I expect per cycle?</span>
            <span class="ml-2 text-gray-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 text-sm text-gray-400">
            Early cycles: 1–3 differences. As you progress, the number increases. The types also change — later cycles introduce higher-impact changes like new objects and damage.
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="group border border-gray-700/50 rounded-lg bg-gray-800/30">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-4 cursor-pointer font-medium hover:bg-gray-800/50 transition-colors text-gray-200">
            <span>Hint: I keep missing differences. What am I doing wrong?</span>
            <span class="ml-2 text-gray-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 text-sm text-gray-400">
            Common issues: rushing through rooms, not establishing a strong baseline, and focusing only on large objects. Small details matter — check floor items, wall positions, and window states.
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="group border border-gray-700/50 rounded-lg bg-gray-800/30">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-4 cursor-pointer font-medium hover:bg-gray-800/50 transition-colors text-gray-200">
            <span>Hint: What's the most important thing to check?</span>
            <span class="ml-2 text-gray-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 text-sm text-gray-400">
            Doors and windows. Even if you miss a visual difference, failing to secure an entry point can end your run. Always prioritize the front door and balcony door.
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="group border border-gray-700/50 rounded-lg bg-gray-800/30">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-4 cursor-pointer font-medium hover:bg-gray-800/50 transition-colors text-gray-200">
            <span>Hint: Are there differences I might not notice?</span>
            <span class="ml-2 text-gray-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 text-sm text-gray-400">
            Yes. Some differences are spoiler-level — they involve things like reflections, hidden doors, or environmental details you might not think to check. Use the spoiler toggle on the Differences Checklist.
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Related -->
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      <a href="/differences-checklist/" class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-gray-700/50 bg-gray-800/50 hover:border-red-700/40 transition-colors text-center">
        <span class="text-2xl block mb-2">🔍</span>
        <span class="font-semibold text-sm text-gray-200">Differences Checklist</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/demo-walkthrough/" class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-gray-700/50 bg-gray-800/50 hover:border-red-700/40 transition-colors text-center">
        <span class="text-2xl block mb-2">🎮</span>
        <span class="font-semibold text-sm text-gray-200">Demo Walkthrough</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/survival-guide/" class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-gray-700/50 bg-gray-800/50 hover:border-red-700/40 transition-colors text-center">
        <span class="text-2xl block mb-2">💀</span>
        <span class="font-semibold text-sm text-gray-200">Survival Guide</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
